  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the author of the OG Web themes (LOT-193), I want to know what gives an account the grey skin's `color_key`, so that HFR-PROTOCOL.md says how a page picks its skin instead of « pending capture ».\n\n### Scope\n\n- #1095 (#728) captured the grey stylesheet (`R728c`) but not what selects it: a logged-in user1 page links the grey key `666666/404550/…`, user2's pages the default `FFFFFF/DEDFDF/…`, and the profile « Thème » option (`theme_css_choice`) does not change the key (user2 test, switched back).\n- The lead: profile page 3 links « Modifier les couleurs du forum », `/setperso.php?config=hfr.inc` (`R55-p3-profile-edit-page3.html:190-191`). Legacy never calls it (`git grep setperso 87fe0d1c`: nothing).\n- One GET of that page: anonymous first, then user2 if it needs a session. **No POST.** Anonymize per docs/FIXTURES.md, independent leak check before the push; record its fields in HFR-PROTOCOL.md « Forum stylesheets ».\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `/setperso.php` captured (anonymous, or user2), committed per FIXTURES.md.\n- [ ] HFR-PROTOCOL.md replaces the « pending capture » sentence with what the page shows (verified or run observation).\n\nNot blocking LOT-193: both stylesheets are captured.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
